  "id": "detroit",
  "intro": "Detroit is the only region on this site where the interesting thing is on the other side of the river. Windsor is a few hundred metres away, which means Canadian broadcast stations come in at full strength, Canadian repeaters are workable from the riverfront, and the Ambassador Bridge and the tunnel are the busiest commercial crossing on the US–Canada border. Add a major airport, the Detroit River carrying lake freighters through the middle of town, and a long-established amateur community, and the band is never empty.",
  "introz": "底特律是本站唯一一个「有意思的东西在河对岸」的地区。温莎就在几百米外，这意味着加拿大的广播电台信号满格、河边就能打通加拿大的中继，而大使桥和隧道是美加边境最繁忙的商业口岸。再加上一个大型机场、穿城而过的五大湖货轮，以及历史悠久的业余无线电社群，频段从不冷清。",
